From: Ken <kvandine@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] selftests/hid: add tests for the Xbox Wireless Controller
 over Bluetooth

The Xbox Wireless Controller model 1708 announces different report
descriptors on Bluetooth Classic firmware (PID 0x02fd) and on BLE
firmware (PID 0x0b20). Replay both descriptors, captured from the same
physical controller before and after a firmware update, through uhid
and check what hid-microsoft makes of them:

 - classic: View (Consumer AC Back) gives KEY_BACK and BTN_SELECT,
   Xbox (Consumer AC Home, report 2) gives KEY_HOMEPAGE and BTN_MODE,
   holding either is not undone by the always-zero Button 11/13 bits,
   and all four codes stay advertised;
 - BLE: View and Xbox are Button 11 and 13 and give BTN_SELECT and
   BTN_MODE only, with KEY_BACK and KEY_HOMEPAGE not advertised;
 - both: Menu gives BTN_START.

